sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI Route
    participant OTPService
    participant Redis
    participant AuthService
    participant UserRepo as UserRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over User,Frontend: Part 1: Verify OTP
    
    User->>+Frontend: Enter OTP code<br/>from email
    Frontend->>+API: POST /auth/verify-otp<br/>{email, otp}
    
    API->>+OTPService: verify_otp(email, otp)
    
    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
        Note over OTPService,Redis: Step 1: Validate OTP
        OTPService->>+UserRepo: get_user_by_email(email)
        UserRepo->>DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?
        DB-->>UserRepo: User
        UserRepo-->>-OTPService: UserDTO
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: GET reset_otp:{user_id}
        Redis-->>-OTPService: Stored OTP or None
        
        alt OTP expired or not found
            OTPService-->>API: HTTPException(400,<br/>"OTP expired or invalid")
            API-->>Frontend: 400 Bad Request
            Frontend-->>User: OTP expired, request new one
        end
        
        alt OTP doesn't match
            OTPService-->>API: HTTPException(400, "Invalid OTP")
            API-->>Frontend: 400 Bad Request
            Frontend-->>User: Incorrect OTP, try again
        end
    end
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 230)
        Note over OTPService,Redis: Step 2: Generate Reset Token
        OTPService->>OTPService: Generate reset token (UUID)
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: SET reset_token:{token} = user_id<br/>EX 900 (15 minutes)
        Redis-->>-OTPService: Token stored
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: DEL reset_otp:{user_id}
        Redis-->>-OTPService: OTP removed
        
        OTPService-->>-API: {reset_token, message}
    end
    
    API-->>-Frontend: 200 OK<br/>{reset_token}
    Frontend-->>-User: ✓ OTP verified!<br/>Enter new password
    
    Note over User,API: ═══════════════════════════════════
    Note over User,Frontend: Part 2: Reset Password
    
    User->>+Frontend: Enter new password
    Frontend->>+API: POST /auth/reset-password<br/>{reset_token, new_password}
    
    API->>+AuthService: reset_password(token, new_password)
    
    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over AuthService,Redis: Step 3: Validate Reset Token
        AuthService->>+Redis: GET reset_token:{token}
        Redis-->>-AuthService: user_id or None
        
        alt Token expired or invalid
            AuthService-->>API: HTTPException(400,<br/>"Invalid/expired token")
            API-->>Frontend: 400 Bad Request
            Frontend-->>User: Token expired,<br/>start over
        end
    end
    
    rect rgb(255, 230, 230)
        Note over AuthService,DB: Step 4: Update Password
        AuthService->>AuthService: hash_password(new_password)<br/>using bcrypt
        
        AuthService->>+UserRepo: update_user_password(user_id, hashed_password)
        UserRepo->>+DB: UPDATE users<br/>SET hashed_password = ?,<br/>updated_at = NOW()<br/>WHERE id = ?
        DB-->>-UserRepo: Updated
        UserRepo-->>-AuthService: Success
        
        AuthService->>+Redis: DEL reset_token:{token}
        Redis-->>-AuthService: Token removed
        
        AuthService->>+Redis: DEL reset_attempts:{user_id}
        Redis-->>-AuthService: Attempts cleared
        
        AuthService-->>-API: {message: "Password reset successfully"}
    end
    
    API-->>-Frontend: 200 OK
    Frontend-->>-User: ✓ Password reset!<br/>You can now log in
